WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.002
 Logan, Keaton,
congratulations.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.437
You guys have made
it to the final round

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:05.605
of this competition.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.373
Now it's time to send you
back to your home forges

00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:13.445
to recreate an iconic weapon
from history, the Japanese ono.

00:00:13.512 --> 00:00:14.447
Oh, yes.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:15.214
Good luck.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:15.982
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:18.384
 Good luck, man.

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:21.054 line:7%
[music playing]

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.555
KEATON: So it's the final round.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:23.656
I'm back here on Nantucket.

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:25.825
I'm going to make
a Japanese ono.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:28.360
So I start by trying to widen
the steel with the drawing

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.731
hammer, and I realize it's going
to make my ax way too thin.

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:32.999
So I take the broad
steel, and I'm

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:35.034
just hitting it into the anvil.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.069
So if I upset it,
it'll get fatter,

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:40.173
and then I can draw it
wider from that thickness.

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:44.343
Not only is it getting
thicker, but I'm

00:00:44.443 --> 00:00:46.612
also starting to get
that crescent shape

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:47.380
that I'm looking for.

00:00:50.182 --> 00:00:51.684
So it's the end of day one.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.854
I got both these ax heads pretty
much completely forged out.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:56.456
I didn't have any oh
[bleep] moments today,

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:57.290
but you never know.

00:00:57.356 --> 00:00:59.392
There could be one coming up.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.094 line:0%
LOGAN: I feel like today's
going to be a good day.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.561 line:0%
I'm gonna go ahead and
clean up the piece.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:05.465 line:0%
I'm gonna set all my weld
lines with the welder

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:07.367 line:0%
and create a scarf
weld so I can bring

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:09.302 line:7%
out more of the head of the ax.

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.270 line:0%
So I'm gonna draw it out
a little bit both ways

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:12.772 line:7%
and see how well they stuck.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.674 line:7%
[hammer pounding]

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:17.143
[machinery ticking]

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:19.779
I start noticing cracks.

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.247
My welds aren't welded up.

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:25.484
And I see I've only got six
[inaudible] of steel left.

00:01:25.584 --> 00:01:27.353
[bleep]

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:28.354
My blade broke.

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:30.623
It shattered.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:34.093
The forge welds never stuck.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.963
The original piece
was all that held on.

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:38.231
I've got to start over.

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:39.766
I've got to find
something to turn in.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.437
I've got plenty of time to at
least turn in something ugly.

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:47.607
So I've got some spring steel,
and we're gonna go from there.

00:01:47.673 --> 00:01:49.242
[hammer pounding]

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:51.043
[machinery whirring]

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:52.311
It's going good.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.380
Tomorrow I have to
finish the small head.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:55.915
I've got to shape the big head.

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:59.085 line:0%
And then the rest the day, I
can start working on the handle.

00:01:59.151 --> 00:02:00.320 line:7%
KEATON: Just started day three.

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:01.721 line:0%
I was not able to
quench last night.

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:03.890
I need to quench this
thing as soon as possible

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:05.258
because I'm running out of time.

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.167
I did it!

00:02:14.233 --> 00:02:16.169
Nice and straight.

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:17.069
Oh, this is great.

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:18.404
Dude, I'm so happy.

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:20.106 line:7%
It's time to do some casting.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.308 line:0%
I'm casting the heart
ornaments that are gonna

00:02:22.374 --> 00:02:24.144 line:7%
go around the holes in the ax.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.713
Artistry and craftsmanship
are very important to me,

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.347
so I want to incorporate that.

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.216
I put some bronze
in the crucible.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:32.551
Get the bronze melting.

00:02:32.618 --> 00:02:34.820
I pull them out, cool
them off in some water.

00:02:34.887 --> 00:02:36.655
This is looking really good.

00:02:36.722 --> 00:02:38.491
Perfect.

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:39.859 line:0%
LOGAN: It's the
morning of day three.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.226 line:0%
It's going OK,
considering the fact

00:02:41.293 --> 00:02:42.661 line:7%
I had to restart yesterday.

00:02:42.728 --> 00:02:44.296
Hopefully just finish
drawing out the little head,

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:46.199
and then start drawing
out the big head.

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:49.669
[hammer tapping]

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:51.837
I've got a small ax head.

00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:53.406
I'm happy with that.

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:55.875
I gotta finish shaping it, and
then move on to the big one.

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:58.144
I'm actually kind of happy
it fell apart at this point.

00:02:58.210 --> 00:02:59.211
It's coming out a lot better.

00:02:59.278 --> 00:03:00.379
It's working a lot better.

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:01.514
I think it was meant to be.

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:05.718
I've almost got the
shape of my head,

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.153
so I'm gonna stick it
in the forge real quick

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.287
and heat it up.

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:08.821
And then we're gonna
go for a quench.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:14.694
Big side first.

00:03:17.329 --> 00:03:19.231
Now we're about to
quench the smaller part.

00:03:19.331 --> 00:03:20.767
Too hot, too hot,
too hot, too hot, too

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:21.801
hot, too hot, too hot, too hot!

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:26.839
Like music to my ears.

00:03:26.905 --> 00:03:28.407
End of day three.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.176
Honestly, I'm just
happy that I'm

00:03:30.242 --> 00:03:31.910
gonna be turning something in.

00:03:31.977 --> 00:03:32.978
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:34.680
Welcome to the kill test.

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:37.917
It's time to find out
what kind of lethal damage

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:39.185
your onos will do.

00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:40.720
To find that out, I
will take your weapon

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.656
and deliver some lethal blows
on this ballistics dummy.

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:46.158
Let's see if your onos
can be an oh, yes.

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:48.160
[chuckles] Logan,
you're up first.

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:48.895
You ready for this?

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:49.662
 Yes, sir.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:53.233
[music playing]

00:04:20.025 --> 00:04:21.527
[laughs]

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:31.170
 Ono!

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:35.208
[laughs] Logan, this
is a lot of fun.

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:39.211
The damage that you did
with your design over here--

00:04:39.311 --> 00:04:41.781
for every chop
using this digs in.

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:43.549
On the way out, it guts you.

00:04:43.615 --> 00:04:45.851
Pretty much opened everything
and crushed everything

00:04:45.951 --> 00:04:47.152
in its path.

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:50.923
More importantly, your
ono is an oh, yes.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:51.957
It will kill.

00:04:52.024 --> 00:04:54.127
 Thank you.

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:54.994
 Keaton, your turn.

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:55.794
So you ready?

00:04:55.861 --> 00:04:56.329
 Oh, yeah.

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:59.632
[music playing]

00:05:28.927 --> 00:05:31.864
 All right, Keaton, let's
talk about your ono here.

00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:34.100
At first when I picked
it up, I was like, oh,

00:05:34.166 --> 00:05:37.336
wow, that's light.

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:40.740
But then when I wielded
it, I was like, oh, yes.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:41.740
This thing stayed on.

00:05:41.807 --> 00:05:43.109
It's solid.

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:47.847
Your edges, they're sharp, and
that's why it dug in very deep.

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:52.017
Overall, sir, your ono was
an oh, yes, and it will kill.

00:05:52.084 --> 00:05:53.953
 Thank you.

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:56.422
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to our strength test,

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:58.357
the bamboo wall chop.

00:05:58.423 --> 00:06:00.593
Now, to push your
onos to the limit,

00:06:00.659 --> 00:06:02.628
I'm gonna beat them
repeatedly against this

00:06:02.728 --> 00:06:05.898
strong, thick, springy bamboo.

00:06:05.964 --> 00:06:08.301
Now, again, it's not what
your onos do to the wall,

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.469
it's what the wall
does to your onos.

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:12.538
Logan, how you feeling?

00:06:12.605 --> 00:06:13.139
 Good.

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:16.041
[music playing]

00:06:16.108 --> 00:06:17.643
 [grunting]

00:06:41.266 --> 00:06:43.335
All right, Logan, good job.

00:06:43.435 --> 00:06:45.170
Your edge is still good.

00:06:45.237 --> 00:06:47.172
Everything's still tight.

00:06:47.272 --> 00:06:48.875
It's heavy.

00:06:48.941 --> 00:06:50.409
The wrap makes it
a little difficult

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:52.878
to slide down during the
chop, but everything's

00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:55.380
still tight, sharp.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:56.849
Did a lot to that.

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:57.349
Good job.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:58.584
 Thank you, sir.

00:06:58.651 --> 00:06:59.818
 Keaton, how you feeling?

00:06:59.918 --> 00:07:00.352
 Good.

00:07:00.419 --> 00:07:01.219
Let's do it.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.822
[music playing]

00:07:03.889 --> 00:07:05.425
 [grunting]

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:23.843
 It's like [inaudible].

00:07:25.143 --> 00:07:26.478
 All right, Keaton, good job.

00:07:26.578 --> 00:07:29.248
It's nice and light,
fast, easy to swing.

00:07:29.315 --> 00:07:32.317
My favorite aspect is how you
had the wood going all the way

00:07:32.417 --> 00:07:34.486
through and split up top here.

00:07:34.553 --> 00:07:35.521
Your edges are still good.

00:07:35.588 --> 00:07:36.856
Everything's tight.

00:07:36.956 --> 00:07:37.856
Good job.

00:07:37.923 --> 00:07:39.424
 Thank you.

00:07:39.491 --> 00:07:40.726
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:43.228
Now it's time to find
out how sharp they are.

00:07:43.328 --> 00:07:44.463
This is the sharpness test--

00:07:44.563 --> 00:07:45.798
the water tube slice.

00:07:45.898 --> 00:07:47.633
Now, unlike the
strength test, this

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:50.870
is all about what your edge
does to those water tubes.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:51.571
Logan, you're up first.

00:07:51.671 --> 00:07:52.371
You ready for this?

00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:53.105
 Yes, sir.

00:07:53.172 --> 00:07:56.676
[music playing]

00:07:59.111 --> 00:08:01.614
[fire sizzling]

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:11.123
 All right, Logan.

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:12.391
That's an impressive cut.

00:08:12.457 --> 00:08:15.594
Very clean, no jagged
edges on the tubes.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.295
Your weapon, sir, it will cut.

00:08:17.396 --> 00:08:18.063
 Thank you, sir.

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:19.465
 Good job.

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:21.133
All right, Keaton, your turn.
So you ready?

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:21.900
 Yep.

00:08:22.001 --> 00:08:25.271
[music playing]

00:08:26.339 --> 00:08:29.842
[fire sizzling]

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:35.781
 All right, Keaton, let's
talk about your weapon here.

00:08:35.848 --> 00:08:37.683
Once again, I have
to mention just

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:41.219
how thin the profile
of your blade is,

00:08:41.286 --> 00:08:42.721
making it razor sharp.

00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:44.289
And the cuts are very clean.

00:08:44.356 --> 00:08:46.759
Overall, sir, it will cut.

00:08:46.859 --> 00:08:47.960
 Thank you.

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:49.595
 All right,
bladesmiths, the judges

00:08:49.695 --> 00:08:51.730
have evaluated
your craftsmanship.

00:08:51.797 --> 00:08:54.667
You've both done incredible work
here today, but only one of you

00:08:54.733 --> 00:08:56.535
can be the Forged
in Fire champion.

00:08:56.635 --> 00:09:00.372
And that champion is--

00:09:00.439 --> 00:09:01.540
Keaton, congratulations.

00:09:01.606 --> 00:09:03.008
You're the Forged
in Fire champion.

00:09:03.108 --> 00:09:05.311
Logan, that is a highly
devastating weapon,

00:09:05.411 --> 00:09:08.414
but at this time I have to ask
you to please shake our hands,

00:09:08.481 --> 00:09:11.483
shake your competitor's hand,
and then please exit the forge.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:13.919
Come on forward, my friend.

00:09:14.019 --> 00:09:16.688
 I'm happy for Keaton,
but I'm disappointed.

00:09:16.755 --> 00:09:18.990
I broke my first blade the
first two days in, so, I mean,

00:09:19.057 --> 00:09:20.893
being able to crank
something out in 23 hours,

00:09:20.993 --> 00:09:22.761
I'm happy with it.

00:09:22.828 --> 00:09:25.697
Moving forward, I'm going
to continue headstrong.

00:09:25.764 --> 00:09:26.865
I may not be a Forged
in Fire champion,

00:09:26.965 --> 00:09:29.935
but I'm happy that I
made great friends.

00:09:30.036 --> 00:09:32.938
 Keaton, that beautifully
crafted and deadly ono

00:09:33.005 --> 00:09:35.707
has earned you the title
of Forged in Fire champion,

00:09:35.774 --> 00:09:38.677
and that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:38.777 --> 00:09:39.478
Good job, brother.

00:09:39.545 --> 00:09:42.248
[applause]

00:09:43.282 --> 00:09:44.517
Is that your smiling face?

00:09:44.617 --> 00:09:45.884
 [laughs]

00:09:45.985 --> 00:09:46.953
 'Cause you look like
you're in pain right now.

00:09:47.019 --> 00:09:47.553
 No, I'm excited.

00:09:47.653 --> 00:09:48.954
 All right.

00:09:49.055 --> 00:09:50.322
Come on forward and shake
our hands, my friend.

00:09:50.422 --> 00:09:52.024
 I'm a Forged in Fire champion.

00:09:52.091 --> 00:09:52.858
I did it.

00:09:52.958 --> 00:09:53.893
This experience has been great.

00:09:53.959 --> 00:09:55.361
It was definitely a challenge.

00:09:55.461 --> 00:09:56.862
The biggest thing I
took away from this

00:09:56.928 --> 00:09:59.531
was just work hard, keep
going, no matter what happens.

00:09:59.632 --> 00:10:03.002
[music playing]

